  "description": "TOPKUH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H82 Co4 Dy3 N6 O32 1+,N1 O3 1-,3(C1 H4 O1),1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.869-4.569 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.72-153.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoIII4DyIII3L4(μ4-O)2(μ-OMe)2(μ1,3-OAc)4(H2O)2(NO3)2]·NO3·3CH3OH·1.5H2O (C61H97N7O40Co4Dy3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
